#
# Trance: keep the icon set in the repository.
#
# The macOS section of most people's global gitignore contains `Icon?` — the
# pattern for Finder's custom-icon resource files, `Icon\r`. It has no slash, so
# it matches any *path component* of that shape, and git on macOS defaults to
# `core.ignorecase=true` on an APFS volume. `icons` is five characters starting
# with "icon". So the whole `src/zen/trance/icons/` tree was ignored, git never
# descended into it, and none of the three packs — several hundred SVG files —
# was ever committed. Nothing reported this: `git status` was clean because the
# files were ignored, and local builds worked because the files were on disk.
#
# A repository `.gitignore` outranks the user's global excludes file, so one
# negation here is enough. It has to name the directory as well as its contents:
# git does not look inside an excluded directory, so un-ignoring only the files
# would never be reached.

!icons/
!icons/**
